{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H2Ebs5FaJiKnRmeBPtpwxq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\ttitle: Overview\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\t# Coconut\n6\t\n7\t## Coconut Context\n8\t\n9\tA living\u00a0[context layer](https://example.invalid/preview)\u00a0that makes every AI interaction (human or agent) smarter. Build it, maintain it, watch your AI's return on investment compound.\n10\t\n11\t* Markdown first (with support for complimentary formats)\n12\t* Designed for both human and agents\n13\t* First class tooling - Web, MCP, CLI, SDK, etc\n14\t* Works out-of-the-box with major clients (Claude, ChatGPT, Copilot, etc)\n15\t* Role-based search / context discovery\n16\t* Enterpr"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"timestamp":"2026-09-09T15:48:42.880Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/example/ripe/corpora/files/products/index.md","content":"---\ntitle: Overview\n---\n\n# Coconut\n\n## Coconut Context\n\nA living\u00a0[context layer](https://example.invalid/preview)\u00a0that makes every AI interaction (human or agent) smarter. Build it, maintain it, watch your AI's return on investment compound.\n\n* Markdown first (with support for complimentary formats)\n* Designed for both human and agents\n* First class tooling - Web, MCP, CLI, SDK, etc\n* Works out-of-the-box with major clients (Claude, ChatGPT, Copilot, etc)\n* Role-based search / context discovery\n* Enterprise authentication (OIDC, OAuth, etc)\n* Agnostic to agentic runtime environment (Claude Managed Agents, OpenAI Workspace Agents, etc)\n* Templates\n\n## Coconut Dashboard\n\nA \"command, control, and communications\" center from which users can carry out the following (in no particular order):\n\n* Provision, manage, and de-provision Coconut instances. On average we predict a given team of 3-5 individuals will have 3-7 coconut instances, but this remains unvalidated\n* Use an assistant to work with the all the coconut instances (it can also manage tasks, knowledge, and context with coconut instances, amongst other things too)\n* Visualize the \"team\" of coconuts and chat with them individually. Also view all their assets (context, knowledge, resources, etc)\n* Create and manage tasks across all the coconut instances. This is for agent tasks only (and has been described as \"jira for agents\")\n* Create \"projects\" that aggregate tasks, knowledge, resources. This is an enabling interface for the AIM methodology (see below)\n\n## Coconut Studio\n\nA web interface used by humans to manage a given Coconut instance. This requires a no-low code level of expertise to use. Beyond the interface to manage the areas mentioned earlier (such as tasks, knowledge, etc) it also includes the following:\n\n* Manage skills (see glossary below)\n* Configure MCP servers\n* Receive email\n* Configure an agent\u2019s A2A identity\n* Use a built in (web) terminal UI\n* Configure notifications to humans (such as to Slack)\n* Manage git configuration (e.g. Github auth)","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}}}
